      "problem": "Calculate $28\\div(7-5)^2.$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS. We start with the **P**arentheses:\n\n$$\n28\\div \\underbrace{(7-5)}_{\\large\\color{blue} 2}{}^2   =28\\div {\\color{blue} 2}^2\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we compute the **E**xponents:\n\n$$\n28\\div\\overbrace{2^2}^{\\large\\color{red} 4} =28\\div {\\color{red} 4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we perform the **D**ivision:\n\n$$\n28\\div 4 =7\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n28\\div(7-5)^2=7.\n$$",
